{"name":"Quicksilver","hex":"#a6a6a6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"quicksilver","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The metal mercury.","An amalgam of mercury and tin applied to the backs of mirrors; quicksilvering."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unpredictable, erratic, or fickle; mercurial."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quicksilver"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mercury (element)","blocks":[{"text":"Mercury is a chemical element; it has symbol Hg and atomic number 80. It is commonly known as quicksilver. A heavy, silvery d-block element, mercury is the only metallic element that is known to be liquid at standard temperature and pressure. As well as having the lowest freezing point, mercury has the lowest boiling point and subsequently the narrowest liquid state range of any metal at standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Pouring_liquid_mercury_bionerd.jpg/330px-Pouring_liquid_mercury_bionerd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercury_(element)"},{"title":"Doyle Lawson","blocks":[{"text":"Doyle Wayne Lawson is an American traditional bluegrass and Southern gospel musician. He is best known as a mandolin player, vocalist, producer, and leader of the 6-man group Doyle Lawson & Quicksilver. Lawson was inducted into the International Bluegrass Music Hall of Fame in 2012."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Doyle_Lawson_and_his_band.jpg/330px-Doyle_Lawson_and_his_band.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doyle_Lawson"},{"title":"Quicksilver (Marvel Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Quicksilver is a character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. Created by artist Jack Kirby and writer Stan Lee, the character first appeared in The X-Men #4. Introduced as an antagonist in Magneto's Brotherhood of Evil Mutants alongside his twin sister, Scarlet Witch, Quicksilver later reformed and joined the Avengers beginning with The Avengers #16, becoming part of the team's second generation."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/28/Quicksilver_%28Marvel_Comics%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quicksilver_(Marvel_Comics)"},{"title":"Quicksilver (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Quicksilver is a 1986 American drama film written and directed by Thomas Michael Donnelly and starring Kevin Bacon. The film, which was distributed by Columbia Pictures, also stars Jami Gertz, Paul Rodriguez, Louie Anderson, Laurence Fishburne, and Rudy Ramos."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d8/Quicksilver_%281986%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quicksilver_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg/500px-Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg/1280px-Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg/500px-Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A round pound coin (density ~7.6 g/cm3) floats on mercury due to the buoyancy force upon it and appears to float higher because of the strong surface tension of the mercury.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Mercury-27128.jpg/500px-Mer